# Video editing mode: open a recording, detect, transcribe, edit, play, export; each step captured for review.
# Needs a display, ffmpeg, and network for the first tiny.en download (just qa-editor Tests/QA/video.qa); not in CI.
# The fixture is build/make-video-fixture.sh's 12 s test pattern: a 440 Hz tone silent from 4 to 6 s, and a sidecar
# with loading from 7 to 9 s and a marker at 10 s. `wait N` counts frames, not seconds (the editor runs at the display
# rate, often 120 fps), so the long steps wait on conditions instead: `wait-for video-jobs` (no waveform, silence,
# transcription or export job left on the tab) and `wait-for video-position` (the playhead has reached a time).
# `video set` changes a Video setting for this run only (QA runs save no settings). Review the PNGs in
# artifacts/qa-editor.
wait-for project 300
mode video
capture video-01-empty
open Tests/QA/Fixtures/video/sample.mp4
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 10
capture video-02-opened
# Silence first, then idle gameplay: each run visibly cuts more (the idle cut, 3.5-9.0 s, takes in the 4-6 s silence
# cut), and the undo below then reverts the idle cut.
command video.detect_silence
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 10
capture video-03-silence
command video.detect_idle
wait 10
capture video-04-idle
video set whisper-model tiny.en
# The first run downloads tiny.en (78 MB) before transcribing.
command video.transcribe
wait-for video-jobs 600
wait 10
capture video-05-transcript
command edit.undo
wait 10
capture video-06-undo
# Undo took the idle cut back: the kept ranges are about 0-4.06 and 5.94-12 s, so past 9.5 s the playhead has crossed
# the silence cut.
command video.play
wait-for video-position 9.5 30
capture video-07-playing
command video.play
mode game
capture video-08-game-mode
mode video
command file.close
cancel
quit
